# Anti-cheat for honest players

## Engine contract (`hanabi/core/game.py`)

- For `BasePlayer` seats, `_notify_players` must **only** call `player.observe(mover, move, observer_view=_get_player_view(observer))`.
- Do **not** add AI-specific belief sync, matrix copy, `hand_cards`, or omniscient align hooks in `Game`.
- Non-cheater `play` receives only `PlayerView` (teammate cards + own hand **size**). Own card identities must never appear in that view.
- Full-info bots use the separate `Cheater` type and `play(GameState)` — never smuggle that into `BasePlayer`.

## Convention channel encode / decode (`hanabi/ai/*`)

- Peer / hand codes used in the mod-8 channel must be functions of **one visible hand + public piles** only (physical / blank belief). Same inputs ⇒ same code for every observer who sees that hand.
- Do not add encode kwargs like `other_hands` / `almost_critical` that make peer codes hinter-asymmetric.
- Each seat updates only rows it can derive from its `PlayerView`: hinter may update teammate rows; non-hinters update **own** row only; hinter never writes own row from their own hint.
- Hinter-only hint **quality** may use both visible hands; keep that in separately named helpers — never feed it into peer codes.
- Prefer `assert_independent_own_decode_matches` (or equivalent) in tests after multi-seat `observe` of a convention hint.

## GUI

- Do not show belief-vs-actual `kind_mismatch` on face-down / own-hidden seats (that leaks private identities to humans).
